{#
  "Edit this text": a town card's text or a region page's lead, proposed by
  anyone signed in (owner 2026-09-30). What it sends is a Text submission in
  the one queue; a curator of the region approves it, or it applies at once
  when a curator writes it inside their own area
  (docs/specs/moderation-and-contribution.md §3.1b).

  The same page shape as /report: dark hero, then the form with the site's
  `.cfield` conventions, from the same stylesheet.

  The current text of the chosen language shows read-only above an empty
  box, so the rider writes their version beside it rather than inside it.
  The language select swaps that quote and the box's live character count
  follows the typing (contribute/place-text.js, a file so the page needs no
  CSP nonce). Without script the select still decides which language the
  text is sent for, and the server enforces the length either way.

  Where the language has a Wikipedia article, the writer says where their
  text comes from: adapted from the article, or their own (two radios,
  required, no default). The server refuses a send without the answer.

  The same page is where a curator of the area corrects a waiting proposal
  (`correcting` set, route moderate_text): the box holds the rider's text,
  the language is the proposal's and cannot change, the rider's note shows
  read-only instead of the note field, and the licence line (addressed to
  the writer) gives way to the lead saying the rider stays credited. There
  the curator either approves the text in the box, with an optional note
  to the writer, or saves the correction and decides later.

  Where the language has a Wikipedia article to credit, the correction page
  asks the curator whether that credit stays (`credit`, owner 2026-10-01):
  two radios and no default, required for Approve only (Save correction
  carries `formnovalidate`), with the writer's own claim as the hint. The
  server refuses an approval without the choice either way.

  A region's "History, nature and culture" text (`target` story, §3.1c) is
  several paragraphs long, so its box starts from the current text of the
  chosen language instead of beside it. It links its sources in place
  (`[words](address)`, explained in the hint). For a language without a
  text, the text of another language (`translate_from`, English first)
  shows above the empty box to translate from. There is no Wikipedia
  question.
#}
{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block head_styles %}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('styles/page/support/report.css') }}">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('styles/page/contribute/place-text.css') }}">
{% endblock %}

{% block body_scripts %}
<script src="{{ asset('contribute/place-text.js') }}" defer></script>
{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
<div class="lhero"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="kicker" style="color:var(--trail)">{{ ('place_text.kicker_' ~ target)|trans }}</div>
  <h1 class="disp">{{ title }}</h1>
  <p class="lead" style="color:rgba(239,230,212,.85);margin-top:.8rem">{{ (correcting|default(null) ? 'place_text.correct.lead' : 'place_text.lead_' ~ target)|trans }}</p>
</div></div>

<section class="pad"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="reppage">
    {% if sent %}
      <div class="csent" role="status">
        <h2>{{ ('place_text.sent_h_' ~ sent)|trans }}</h2>
        <p>{{ ('place_text.sent_p_' ~ sent)|trans }}</p>
        <p>{{ 'place_text.sent_ref'|trans({'%ref%': reference}) }}</p>
        <p><a href="{{ back }}">{{ ('place_text.back_' ~ target)|trans }}</a> &middot;
           <a href="{{ path('profile') }}">{{ 'place_text.follow'|trans }}</a></p>
      </div>
    {% else %}
      {# A region has two texts with two purposes (§3.1b, §3.1c): geography,
         and history, nature and culture. The form says which one this is,
         links the writer to the other, and reminds a curator before they
         approve. A town card has one text, so no note. #}
      {% if target in ['region', 'story'] %}
        <div class="cnote pt-purpose" role="note"><p>
          {{- (correcting ? 'place_text.purpose_' ~ target ~ '_correct' : 'place_text.purpose_' ~ target)|trans -}}
          {%- if other and not correcting %} <a href="{{ other }}">{{ ('place_text.purpose_go_' ~ (target == 'region' ? 'story' : 'region'))|trans }}</a>{% endif -%}
        </p></div>
      {% endif %}
      {# Why a curator's own pen sent them here: the town lies outside their areas. #}
      {% for m in app.flashes('notice') %}<div class="cnote" role="status"><p>{{ m|trans }}</p></div>{% endfor %}
      {% if error %}
        <div class="cerr" role="alert">{{ error|trans({'%max%': max}|merge(error_params)) }}</div>
      {% endif %}

      {% set story = target == 'story' %}
      <form method="post" action="{{ action }}" id="place-text-form"{% if story %} class="pt-story-form"{% endif %}
            data-texts="{{ texts|json_encode }}"
            {% if story and not correcting %}data-story data-langs="{{ langs|json_encode }}"{% endif %}
            {% if articles is not null %}data-articles="{{ articles|json_encode }}"{% endif %}>
        <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token(csrf_id) }}">
        {% for k, v in hidden %}<input type="hidden" name="{{ k }}" value="{{ v }}">{% endfor %}

        <div class="cfield">
          <label for="pt-lang">{{ 'place_text.field_lang'|trans }}</label>
          <select id="pt-lang" name="lang"{{ correcting ? ' disabled' }}>
            {% for code, label in langs %}
              <option value="{{ code }}"{{ code == lang ? ' selected' }}>{{ label }}</option>
            {% endfor %}
          </select>
        </div>

        {% set current = texts[lang] ?? '' %}
        {% if story and not correcting %}
          {% set from = translate_from|default(null) %}
          <figure class="pt-current pt-translate" id="pt-translate"{{ from is null ? ' hidden' }}>
            <figcaption id="pt-translate-h" data-words="{{ 'place_text.translate_h'|trans({'%lang%': '%lang%'}) }}">{{ from ? 'place_text.translate_h'|trans({'%lang%': langs[from] ?? from}) }}</figcaption>
            <blockquote id="pt-translate-text">{{ from ? texts[from] }}</blockquote>
          </figure>
        {% else %}
        <figure class="pt-current" id="pt-current">
          <figcaption>{{ 'place_text.current_h'|trans }}</figcaption>
          <blockquote id="pt-current-text"{{ current is empty ? ' hidden' }}>{{ current }}</blockquote>
          <p class="chint" id="pt-current-none"{{ current is not empty ? ' hidden' }}>{{ 'place_text.current_none'|trans }}</p>
        </figure>
        {% endif %}

        <div class="cfield{{ story ? ' pt-editor' }}">
          <label for="pt-text">{{ 'place_text.field_text'|trans }} <span class="req" aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
          {# A history text's links, made easy to place and to see (§3.1c):
             a button that wraps the selected words in a link, colours behind
             the link words and the address in the box, and a list of the
             links under it. All drawn by place-text.js; hidden until it
             runs, so without script the box is a plain box. #}
          {% if story %}
            <div class="pt-linkbar" id="pt-linkbar" hidden>
              <button type="button" class="btn btn-g pt-link-open" id="pt-link-open" aria-controls="pt-link-form" aria-expanded="false">{{ 'place_text.link_add'|trans }}</button>
              <div class="pt-link-form" id="pt-link-form" hidden>
                <label for="pt-link-url">{{ 'place_text.link_url'|trans }}</label>
                <input type="url" id="pt-link-url" inputmode="url" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" placeholder="https://">
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-p" id="pt-link-insert">{{ 'place_text.link_insert'|trans }}</button>
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-g" id="pt-link-cancel">{{ 'place_text.cancel'|trans }}</button>
              </div>
              <p class="chint pt-link-msg" id="pt-link-msg" role="status" aria-live="polite"
                 data-select="{{ 'place_text.link_select_first'|trans }}"
                 data-bad-url="{{ 'place_text.link_bad_url'|trans }}"
                 data-for="{{ 'place_text.link_for'|trans({'%words%': '%words%'}) }}"></p>
            </div>
          {% endif %}
          <div class="{{ story ? 'pt-hl-wrap' }}">
            <textarea id="pt-text" name="text" required maxlength="{{ raw_max }}"{% if story %} rows="16" data-links data-generic="{{ generic_anchors|json_encode }}"{% endif %} aria-describedby="pt-text-hint pt-text-count">{{ text }}</textarea>
          </div>
          {% if story %}
            {# Each link's check (website gate + Safe Browsing) as it appears,
               from `story_link_check`: the same verdicts a send meets. #}
            <div class="pt-links" id="pt-links" hidden
                 data-h="{{ 'place_text.links_h'|trans({'%count%': '%count%'}) }}"
                 data-generic-note="{{ 'place_text.links_generic'|trans }}"
                 data-check-url="{{ path('story_link_check') }}"
                 data-check-token="{{ csrf_token(link_check_csrf_id) }}"
                 data-st-checking="{{ 'place_text.link_st_checking'|trans }}"
                 data-st-ok="{{ 'place_text.link_st_ok'|trans }}"
                 data-st-dead="{{ 'place_text.link_st_dead'|trans }}"
                 data-st-parked="{{ 'place_text.link_st_parked'|trans }}"
                 data-st-unsafe="{{ 'place_text.link_st_unsafe'|trans }}"
                 data-st-unknown="{{ 'place_text.link_st_unknown'|trans }}"
                 data-st-limit="{{ 'place_text.link_st_limit'|trans }}">
              <p class="pt-links-h" id="pt-links-h"></p>
              <ol id="pt-links-list"></ol>
            </div>
            {# A link that is not plainly fine never blocks the text: the writer,
               and the curator approving it, confirm by hand that they opened it
               (StoryLinkCheck, §3.1c). Shown by place-text.js when a link is
               not "Checked: OK"; shown by the server when a send came back
               for want of it. #}
            {% set links_refused = error == 'place_text.error.links_unconfirmed' %}
            <label class="cinline pt-links-ok{{ links_refused ? ' is-asked' }}" id="pt-links-ok" for="pt-links-confirm"{{ not links_refused ? ' hidden' }}>
              <input type="checkbox" id="pt-links-confirm" name="links_confirmed" value="1">
              <span>{{ 'place_text.links_confirm'|trans }}</span>
            </label>
          {% endif %}
          <p class="chint pt-count" id="pt-text-count" aria-live="polite" data-max="{{ max }}"
             data-words="{{ 'place_text.count'|trans({'%count%': '%count%', '%max%': max}) }}">{{ 'place_text.count'|trans({'%count%': text|length, '%max%': max}) }}</p>
          {# How to write a history text, as steps beside the box on a wide
             screen and under it on a narrow one (place-text.css). The link
             example wears the box's own tints, then shows how the page
             reads it, so the markup is learned by sight. #}
          {% if story %}
            <aside class="pt-howto" id="pt-text-hint">
              <p class="pt-howto-h">{{ 'place_text.howto_h'|trans }}</p>
              <ol>
                <li>{{ 'place_text.howto_whole'|trans({'%max%': max|number_format(0, '.', ',')}) }}</li>
                <li>{{ 'place_text.howto_paragraph'|trans }}</li>
                <li>{{ 'place_text.howto_cite'|trans }}
                  {# The example in the page's own language: its words and address are messages too. #}
                  {% set ex_words = 'place_text.howto_ex_words'|trans %}
                  <code class="pt-howto-ex"><mark class="w">[{{ ex_words }}]</mark><mark class="u">({{ 'place_text.howto_ex_url'|trans }})</mark></code>
                  {{ 'place_text.howto_reads'|trans }} <span class="pt-howto-link">{{ ex_words }}</span></li>
                <li>{{ 'place_text.howto_words'|trans }}</li>
                <li>{{ 'place_text.howto_sites'|trans }}</li>
              </ol>
            </aside>
          {% else %}
            <p class="chint" id="pt-text-hint">{{ 'place_text.field_text_hint'|trans }}</p>
          {% endif %}
        </div>

        {# Where the writer's text comes from: a required choice of two, with no
           default, asked only for a language with an article to adapt and
           checked again on the server. Hidden and disabled for a language
           without one, so its `required` never blocks the send. It is the
           writer's claim only; the approving curator decides the credit.
           Not shown when a curator corrects a proposal (`articles` null):
           their own credit choice decides there. #}
        {% if articles is not null %}
          {% set has_article = articles[lang] ?? false %}
          <fieldset class="cpick pt-pick pt-source" id="pt-source"{{ not has_article ? ' hidden disabled' }}>
            <legend>{{ 'place_text.field_source'|trans }} <span class="req" aria-hidden="true">*</span></legend>
            <label class="cinline" for="pt-source-adapted">
              <input type="radio" id="pt-source-adapted" name="derived" value="adapted" required{{ source == 'adapted' ? ' checked' }}>
              <span>{{ 'place_text.field_derived'|trans }}</span>
            </label>
            <label class="cinline" for="pt-source-own">
              <input type="radio" id="pt-source-own" name="derived" value="own" required{{ source == 'own' ? ' checked' }}>
              <span>{{ 'place_text.field_own'|trans }}</span>
            </label>
          </fieldset>
        {% endif %}

        {% if credit %}
          <fieldset class="cpick pt-pick pt-credit" id="pt-credit" aria-describedby="pt-credit-hint">
            <legend>{{ 'place_text.correct.credit_legend'|trans }} <span class="req" aria-hidden="true">*</span></legend>
            <label class="cinline" for="pt-credit-keep">
              <input type="radio" id="pt-credit-keep" name="credit" value="keep" required{{ credit.choice == 'keep' ? ' checked' }}>
              <span>{{ 'place_text.correct.credit_keep'|trans }}</span>
            </label>
            <label class="cinline" for="pt-credit-drop">
              <input type="radio" id="pt-credit-drop" name="credit" value="drop" required{{ credit.choice == 'drop' ? ' checked' }}>
              <span>{{ 'place_text.correct.credit_drop'|trans }}</span>
            </label>
            <p class="chint" id="pt-credit-hint">{{ 'place_text.correct.credit_hint'|trans }}</p>
            {% if credit.claim is not null %}
              <p class="chint pt-credit-claim" id="pt-credit-claim">{{ 'place_text.correct.credit_claim'|trans({'%choice%': (credit.claim ? 'place_text.field_derived' : 'place_text.field_own')|trans}) }}</p>
            {% endif %}
          </fieldset>
        {% endif %}

        {% if correcting %}
          {% if correcting.note %}
            <figure class="pt-current" id="pt-rider-note">
              <figcaption>{{ 'place_text.correct.note_h'|trans }}</figcaption>
              <blockquote>{{ correcting.note }}</blockquote>
            </figure>
          {% endif %}
          <div class="cfield">
            <label for="pt-reply">{{ 'place_text.correct.reply_label'|trans }}</label>
            <textarea id="pt-reply" name="reply" rows="3" maxlength="{{ reply_max }}" aria-describedby="pt-reply-hint">{{ reply }}</textarea>
            <p class="chint" id="pt-reply-hint">{{ 'place_text.correct.reply_hint'|trans }}</p>
          </div>
        {% else %}
          <div class="cfield">
            <label for="pt-note">{{ 'place_text.field_note'|trans }}</label>
            <input type="text" id="pt-note" name="note" maxlength="{{ note_max }}" aria-describedby="pt-note-hint">
            <p class="chint" id="pt-note-hint">{{ 'place_text.field_note_hint'|trans }}</p>
          </div>
        {% endif %}

        <div class="pt-actions">
          {% if correcting %}
            <button type="submit" name="do" value="approve" class="btn btn-p">{{ 'place_text.correct.approve'|trans }}</button>
            {# Saving a correction leaves the decision, and the credit question, for later. #}
            <button type="submit" name="do" value="save" class="btn btn-g" formnovalidate>{{ 'place_text.correct.submit'|trans }}</button>
          {% else %}
            <button type="submit" class="btn btn-p">{{ 'place_text.submit'|trans }}</button>
          {% endif %}
          <a class="btn btn-g" href="{{ back }}">{{ 'place_text.cancel'|trans }}</a>
        </div>
        {# Small print under the buttons: the terms of sending, not a field. #}
        {% if not correcting %}<p class="pt-licence">{{ 'place_text.licence'|trans|rich }}</p>{% endif %}
      </form>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</div></section>
{% endblock %}
